From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kholin <oodzchen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:18:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro: reserve bootloader
 splash framebuffer

ABL leaves the DPU continuously scanning out the 3392x2400 bootloader
framebuffer at 0xfc800000..0xfe70dfff (31,800 KiB) at 144 Hz until
drm/msm tears down bootloader scanout at ~0.48 s. Without matching the
stock splash_region reservation (0xfc800000, size 0x2b00000), Linux
exposes 0xfc800000..0xff7fffff as System RAM and places both the 32 MiB
global CMA pool (0xfcc00000..0xfebfffff) and adsp-rpc-remote-heap
(0xfec00000..0xff7fffff) directly on top of the active scanout range.

During early boot (~0.35-0.36 s, before drm/msm stops scanout),
qcom_scm_pas_init_image() for soccp/adsp calls dma_alloc_coherent(),
which allocates 4K metadata pages out of global CMA (0xfcc00000+) and
hands them to TrustZone. TZ enables XPU memory protection on those pages
during the SCM call; whenever the 144 Hz DPU scanout DMA (or an active
efifb console) accesses that page while XPU-locked, the resulting
hardware XPU violation triggers an immediate silent SoC reset.

Reserve 0xfc800000..0xff2fffff as no-map (matching the stock ColorOS DT)
so Linux places global CMA and adsp-rpc-remote-heap safely below
0xf3800000, completely outside the active bootloader framebuffer.

Co-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@deepmind.google>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts  | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,21 @@
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * ABL leaves DPU scanning out the 3392x2400 framebuffer at
+		 * 0xfc800000 until drm/msm tears down bootloader scanout
+		 * (~0.48 s). Matching the stock splash_region reservation
+		 * (0xfc800000, 0x2b00000) prevents Linux from placing global
+		 * CMA (0xfcc00000) and adsp-rpc-remote-heap inside the live
+		 * scanout range, where qcom_scm_pas_init_image() DMA metadata
+		 * allocations get XPU-locked by TZ and trigger an immediate
+		 * hardware reset on DPU/efifb access.
+		 */
+		splash_mem: splash@fc800000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0xfc800000 0x0 0x2b00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		ramoops@bfff00000 {
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0xb 0xfff00000 0x0 0x100000>;
-- 
2.47.0
